# ubs ignore globs (read by default as PROJECT/.ubsignore).
#
# bd-yxsqo: UBS Meta-Runner v5.3.11 hangs (>10 min, superlinear) on very large
# Rust files — even a single explicit file, and even with --skip-type-narrowing.
# Measured 2026-08-17: connection.rs (270k lines) and pager.rs (55k lines) both
# time out at >90s; the pathology kicks in somewhere below 55k lines. A `git diff`
# that touches any of these makes `ubs $(git diff --name-only)` hang and blocks the
# agent. These files are excluded here so ubs skips them in every mode (`ubs .`,
# `ubs --diff`, `ubs --staged`, and explicit-file scans — all verified to skip).
#
# Coverage note: these files still get clippy + `cargo check` + the test suites;
# only the ubs pass is skipped. Shrinking them (esp. the connection.rs god-object,
# bd-oxw4d) restores ubs coverage. If a NEW ubs scan hangs, the file is likely too
# big — add it here.
crates/fsqlite-core/src/connection.rs
crates/fsqlite-pager/src/pager.rs
crates/fsqlite-vdbe/src/codegen.rs
